{"type":"message","id":"448ceb60","parentId":"184d6e64","timestamp":"2026-05-26T21:46:03.971Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"It seems the POST /send endpoint is giving 1101 errors consistently. The GET endpoints work fine with X-API-Key header. The issue seems to be with the POST endpoint itself, not authentication. This could be a bug in the Cloudflare Worker, or the endpoint might expect a different request format.\n\nLet me try a different approach - perhaps the endpoint needs the API key in a query parameter, or there's a rate limit issue, or the body format is slightly different.\n\nLet me check if maybe I need to URL-encode the content or something.\n\nActually, wait - looking at the error code 1101 - that seems to be a Cloudflare specific error code. Let me check what 1101 is on Cloudflare. Error 1101 typically means \"Worker thrown exception\" or \"Worker exceeded resources\". \n\nLet me try a simpler approach - perhaps the issue is with how the Worker is handling the request body. Let me try with a very minimal payload and see if the Worker itself is crashing.\n\nSince the Worker is returning \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" on GET requests but failing on POST with 1101, this suggests the Worker itself might be crashing when trying to parse the request body or process the send action.\n\nLet me try a few more things to diagnose, and then report the status. Since I cannot successfully send messages via POST, I'll document what I found and the issue with the send endpoint.\n","thinkingSignature":"d25584797a310d6babf7221d524beb814b25b194f4eae63515b849db1eb9a690"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0knxzlhd32uo_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n  -d \"test\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":112,"o