{"type":"message","id":"d1dec4bc","parentId":"8c12d0fc","timestamp":"2026-05-26T21:46:08.856Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST /send endpoint seems to be throwing 1101 consistently, while GET /history works fine. This could be a Cloudflare Worker issue (1101 is typically \"Worker threw exception\" in Cloudflare). Let me check if there's a specific format expected.\n\nLet me try to understand what's happening. The GET endpoints work fine (authenticated with X-API-Key header), but POST /send returns 1101 (Worker exception). This suggests the Cloudflare Worker itself has a bug or the endpoint expects different formatting.\n\nLet me try posting to a different endpoint or with different parameters.\n","thinkingSignature":"e95faa4ad4c5131c48b9336098d667792eaae79586ddcf8225dcb38e85fe4809"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qasmietmafej_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=1\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qasmietmafej_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat test\",\"type\":\"message\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":104,"output":278,"cacheRead":22598,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22980,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779831964223,"responseId":"0665479c7c356b591b19dfe6affd0b45"}}
